{
  "description": "How a runner must classify each typed daemon refusal in this directory (<code>.json, generated from the real TypeScript builders by scripts/generate-refusal-wire-fixtures.ts). wait = wait for the device within the bounded device wait; acquire-new-session = retry under a fresh session UUID; retry = ordinary bounded retry; fail = fail the attempt. Precedence when a runner derives it: wait, then acquire-new-session (nextAction), then retry (retryable: true), else fail. knownGaps maps a runner (kotlin, swift) to the disposition it currently produces instead of the expected one, so the suite stays green while the gap is tracked; a gap that starts matching the expectation fails the suite until the entry is removed. fields is what a runner must read from the fixture's wire payload: the typed code, retryable, whether nextAction is acquire_new_session, a positive retryAfterMs hint, and (capacity refusals) the externalDevices and iOS heldDevices that count against the limit. dbPath and unknownMigrations are also listed among the fields, but only the TypeScript contract readers check them. A field absent from a row is absent on the wire. session_held_by_recovery waits when retryable; device_unhealthy waits only when retryable and recovering are true. fields.recovering pins the wire boolean when present.",
